KG42.register("rules-491b4977411f4e8d65dfb495",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R003","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Prosumers must submit their descending bidding curves for energy trading to the LMO. Scope: First-stage prosumer bidding for the local P2P energy market. Prosumers must submit their ascending offering curves for energy trading to the LMO. Scope: First-stage prosumer bidding for the local P2P energy market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"First-stage prosumer bidding for the local P2P energy market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X001","symbol":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Energy quantities of offering (the offered P2P energy block) of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario/block omega; the submitted offering curve formed by these quantities must be ascending in the predicted LEM price ordering (source Eq. (12), the submitted-curve requirement of constraint C002).","kind":"operational","domain":"Continuous first-stage decision quantity (P2P energy quantity offered), one value per prosumer j, time slot t and scenario/block omega; the cited evidence states no explicit numeric bounds for this symbol itself.","unit":null,"indices":["j = prosumer","t = time slot","\\omega, \\omega' = scenarios (offering/bidding blocks)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X002","symbol":"P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Energy quantities of bidding (the bid P2P energy block) of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario/block omega; the submitted bidding curve formed by these quantities must be descending in the predicted LEM price ordering (source Eq. (13), the submitted-curve requirement of constraint C001).","kind":"operational","domain":"Continuous first-stage decision quantity (P2P energy quantity bid), one value per prosumer j, time slot t and scenario/block omega; the cited evidence states no explicit numeric bounds for this symbol itself.","unit":null,"indices":["j = prosumer","t = time slot","\\omega, \\omega' = scenarios (offering/bidding blocks)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e11"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T001","symbol":"\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Predicted energy trading price in the LEM for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario omega; the source explicitly identifies it as a parameter (input) of the prosumer's decision problem, and it is the ordering quantity that appears as the guard condition in Eqs. (12)-(13) for the submitted curves.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["j = prosumer","t = time slot","\\omega = scenario"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers must submit their descending bidding curves for energy trading to the LMO. Scope: First-stage prosumer bidding for the local P2P energy market.","expression":"P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} \\leq P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t   (13)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers must submit their ascending offering curves for energy trading to the LMO. Scope: First-stage prosumer bidding for the local P2P energy market.","expression":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} \\geq P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t   (12)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"A.S. Gazafroudi et al. load constraints in which its total energy reduction must be equal to w energ","equation_id":"(12)-(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Finally, prosumers must submit their ascending offering and descending bidding curves for energy tradings to the LMO. Thus, optimal offering and bidding blocks are given by Eqs. (12) and (13) based on [31], respectively: P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} \\geq P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t   (12)   P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} \\leq P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}, \\forall \\omega \\geq \\omega', \\forall j, \\forall t   (13) where both \\omega and \\omega' represent scenarios (offering/bidding blocks). In other words, Eqs. (12) and (13) guarantees that optimal offering and bidding curves are ascending and descending, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-en3","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p02-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":"2","section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"𝑡 g g 𝜆−𝑡 ToU buying price from the grid at time slot 𝑡 𝐿𝑗 Maximum energy consumption for pro- sumer","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Parameters in the first stage: \\beta_{jt} Portion of interruptible loads for prosumer j at time slot t which is between 0 and 1; \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} Predicted energy trading price in the LEM for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; \\lambda^{+}_{t} ToU selling price to the grid at time slot t; \\lambda^{-}_{t} ToU buying price from the grid at time slot t; \\bar{L}_{j} Maximum energy consumption for prosumer j; \\bar{P}_{j} Maximum energy generation (PV capacity) for prosumer j; \\rho_{\\omega} Probability of scenario \\omega; L_{jt\\omega} Energy consumption for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P_{jt\\omega} Energy generation for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega. Variables in the first stage: \\lambda^{p2p}_{jit} The price of P2P energy trading between prosumers j and i at time slot t; \\lambda^{b}_{jtm} Bidding price of prosumer j in block m and time t; \\lambda^{o}_{jtm} Offering price of prosumer j in block m and time t; O_{jt} Offer vector for prosumer j at time t; B_{jt} Bid vector for prosumer j at time t; B_{jtm} Bidding quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t; O_{jtm} Offering quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t; EC^{p}_{j} Expected cost for prosumer j; EP^{p}_{j} Expected profit for prosumer j; Lf,i_{jt\\omega} The amount of interruptible load for prosumer j at time t and scenario \\omega; Lf,s_{jt\\omega} The amount of shiftable load for prosumer j at time t and scenario \\omega; OF^{p}_{j} Objective function for prosumer j; P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} The quantity of offering for P2P trading among prosumers j and i at time slot t and block m; P^{p2p,+}_{jit} Energy that prosumer j sells to prosumer i at time slot t; P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm} The quantity of bidding for P2P trading among prosumers j and i at time slot t and block m; P^{p2p,-}_{jit} Energy that prosumer j buys from prosumer i at time slot t; P^{+}_{jt\\omega} Total energy sold of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{-}_{jt\\omega} Total energy purchased of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega} Energy sold to the grid at ToU price by prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega} Energy purchased from the grid at ToU price to prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} Energy quantities of offering for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} Energy quantities of bidding for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; u_{jit} A binary variable representing P2P trading status between prosumers j and i at time slot t; v_{jt\\omega} A binary variable for expressing status of buying/selling in the LEM of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"𝑗 𝑗 𝑗, respectively. Moreover, Eqs. (2) and (3) express expected cost and 𝑃𝑗 profit for prosumer 𝑗, ","equation_id":"(2)-(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Moreover, Eqs. (2) and (3) express expected cost and profit for prosumer j, respectively. EC^{p}_{j} = \\sum_{t\\omega} \\rho_{\\omega}(\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} + \\lambda^{-}_{t} P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}), \\forall j   (2)   EP^{p}_{j} = \\sum_{t\\omega} \\rho_{\\omega}(\\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} + \\lambda^{+}_{t} P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}), \\forall j   (3). According to Eq. (2), the expected cost for player j includes two terms. The first term, \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}, represents the expected cost of energy trading with other prosumers in LEM in scenario \\omega and time t. The expected cost of energy bought from the grid is represented in the second term, \\lambda^{-}_{t} P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}. Moreover, Eq. (3) consist of two terms. The first term, \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}, states the expected profit of energy trading in the LEM, and the second term, \\lambda^{+}_{t} P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}, states the expected profit of energy sold to the grid. Here, \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} is a parameter (input) of the proposed decision making problem for prosumer j representing energy trading price in the LEM."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","quote":"Finally, prosumers must submit their ascending offering and descending bidding curves for energy tradings to the LMO."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","quote":"Finally, prosumers must submit their ascending offering and descending bidding curves for energy tradings to the LMO."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5e74bd2af8bbbcd2fabcb766a9528eddd137e3e3f612fa7246aa3a7f26440452","applicability":"formalized","reason":"R003 is the coordination-stage rule of mechanism v141-a-M01 whose frozen content is the submission of prosumer curves to the LMO: edge E001 (bidding.demand -links-> coordination.local_operator) and edge E002 (bidding.supply -links-> coordination.local_operator), both grounded in the rule's own formula evidence v141-b-g02-e11. That evidence contains the operative mathematics of the submission: Eqs. (12)-(13) require the offered P2P quantities P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} to be non-decreasing and the bid P2P quantities P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} to be non-increasing as the predicted LEM price lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} and the scenario/block order (omega >= omega') increase, i.e. ascending offering and descending bidding curves, exactly as the frozen statements of C001 and C002 assert. C001 and C002 are therefore formalized by faithful transcription of Eqs. (13) and (12) respectively (formalization_origin=source); their constraint_id, statement, role, members and original evidence_ids are preserved unchanged, and their kind is left 'procedural' because the obligation this rule owns is the submission to the LMO, whose required curve shape is now given mathematically. Two first-stage operational decision quantities (X001 = P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}, X002 = P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}) and one parameter (T001 = lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega}, explicitly called 'a parameter (input) of the proposed decision making problem for prosumer j' in v141-b-g02-e04) are declared with the source scope (prosumer j, time slot t, scenario/block omega); omega, omega', j and t are indices, not variables or parameters. No unit is stated for these symbols in the nomenclature evidence, so units are left null rather than inferred. All B evidence used here remains UNREVIEWED in this experiment; this formalization is provisional and does not assert that B transcription or downstream science has passed source review.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001"],"rationale":"Constraint C001 is the descending-bidding-curve requirement carried by frozen edge E001 (bidding.demand -links-> coordination.local_operator, evidence v141-b-g02-e11): the bid-side quantity P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} required to be non-increasing in the predicted LEM price ordering is the content of the demand/bidding curve that must be submitted to the LMO."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E002"],"rationale":"Constraint C002 is the ascending-offering-curve requirement carried by frozen edge E002 (bidding.supply -links-> coordination.local_operator, evidence v141-b-g02-e11): the offer-side quantity P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} required to be non-decreasing in the predicted LEM price ordering is the content of the supply/offering curve that must be submitted to the LMO."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-X001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E002"],"rationale":"X001 (P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}) is the offered P2P energy quantity defined for each prosumer, time slot and scenario/block; it is the supply-side object whose ordered values form the offering curve submitted along E002 (bidding.supply -> coordination.local_operator)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-X002","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001"],"rationale":"X002 (P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}) is the bid P2P energy quantity defined for each prosumer, time slot and scenario/block; it is the demand-side object whose ordered values form the bidding curve submitted along E001 (bidding.demand -> coordination.local_operator)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-T001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001","v141-c-R003-E002"],"rationale":"T001 (lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega}) is the predicted LEM trading price, an exogenous input to the prosumer's decision problem (explicitly called a parameter in v141-b-g02-e04); it is the ordering quantity shared by both submitted curve branches, so it is bound to the demand and supply bidding nodes and to the LMO/coordination node, through the two submission edges E001 and E002."}],"revision_requests":["Block-index consistency (B re-extraction): evidence v141-b-g02-e11 states 'where both \\omega and \\omega' represent scenarios (offering/bidding blocks)', while the nomenclature (v141-b-g01-en2) defines m as 'Offer and bid blocks for prosumers' and Eqs. (14)-(15) index submitted blocks by m. Before the Eqs. (12)-(13) ordering property is applied to the submitted block vectors O_{jt}/B_{jt}, B should confirm whether the block index in Eqs. (12)-(13) is m (with omega only a scenario label) or whether the source genuinely equates scenario and block indices.","Units (B re-extraction): the nomenclature evidence v141-b-g01-en3 states no unit for P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}, P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} or lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega}, and Table 1 (v141-b-g02-e33, a different symbol Pbar_j) is the only place a '(kWh)' label appears. Unit annotations for the first-stage energy quantities and the LEM/ToU prices must be extracted and verified before quantitative use; units are left null here rather than inferred.","Quantifier form: in Eqs. (12)-(13) the clause '\\forall \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} \\geq \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega'}' reads as an ordering guard rather than a quantification over a variable. The expression set on C001/C002 keeps it verbatim from the source; B verification should confirm the intended reading (blocks ordered by the predicted LEM price) as supported by the following sentence 'Eqs. (12) and (13) guarantees that optimal offering and bidding curves are ascending and descending, respectively'.","Unreviewed evidence (scope note, not a graph defect): the evidence used here (v141-b-g02-e11, v141-b-g01-en3, v141-b-g02-e04) is B-transcribed and UNREVIEWED in this experiment; no source audit, C2 review or Agent E validation has been performed, so the transcribed equations and symbol definitions remain candidate support only. The frozen graph (V, E, mechanism, stage, members and evidence of C001/C002) is adequate for this formalization; no C.1 graph revision is requested."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
